        "original_id": "af8c14cf-6339-576c-b3bf-cb0cc981be21",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Chelidonium majus, Duranta, Stylophorum diphyllum\n- Taxonomy: Chelidonium, Verbenaceae\n- Topics: common names, genus relationships\n\nFacts:\n- Chelidonium majus is commonly known as greater celandine, tetterwort, nipplewort, or swallowwort.\n- The name tetterwort can also refer to Sanguinaria canadensis.\n- Chelidonium majus is a herbaceous perennial plant and the only species in the genus Chelidonium.\n- Duranta is a genus of flowering plants in the verbena family, Verbenaceae.\n- The common name of Stylophorum diphyllum is derived from greater celandine, Chelidonium majus.\n- Chelidonium majus is a closely related European plant with similarly shaped leaves and similarly coloured and shaped flowers to Stylophorum diphyllum.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
